From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shelley Vohr <shelley.vohr@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 14:20:39 +0000
Subject: deps: use posix_spawn for child processes on Linux (libuv backport)

libuv only took its posix_spawn() path on Apple platforms, so on Linux
every uv_spawn() forked the calling process. In an Electron main process
(1.5 TB of address space reserved for the V8 sandbox and pointer cages)
that fork costs 2-3 ms of main-thread time per child_process.spawn() /
execFile() for the page-table copy alone; with posix_spawn
(clone(CLONE_VM|CLONE_VFORK)) it is ~0.6 ms and independent of the
parent's size.

This is the series that landed on libuv's v1.x branch after 1.52.1 and
will ship in libuv 1.53; drop this patch once Electron's Node carries a
libuv that has it:
  58418d53 process: better validation for process->pid usage (#3539) (Jameson Nash)
  1f56978a unix: check return value of fcntl call (#5089) (Ben Noordhuis)
  40d45efe unix: use posix_spawn instead of fork (#3520) (Jameson Nash)
  79b923ea aix,ibmi: fix undeclared identifiers (#5123) (Sravani Gundepalli, Korinne Adler)
  4522bfb9 process,unix: avoid off-by-one in uv__spawn_resolve_and_spawn (#5150) (Jameson Nash)

